Capture guards: every screenshot and snapshot text the server hands out passes
through the guards plugins register, so a plugin can keep what must not leave
the browser out of all of them (the vault-frames plugin masks the fields a
vault fill wrote, ./vault-frames-plugin/mask.js). A guard that throws refuses
the capture: the route answers 409 capture_refused, never the unguarded data.

- every page.screenshot of a route (screenshot, snapshot includeScreenshot,
  the legacy /snapshot) goes through captureScreenshot, never to a file;
- the accessibility snapshot (iframes included), the Google SERP text and the
  page structure go through captureText before they are cached or returned;
- GET /tabs/:id/screenshot also answers X-Camofox-Viewport (CSS width,
  height, scrollX, scrollY) for a coordinate click on what it shows;
- plugins get registerCaptureGuard, captureScreenshot and CaptureRefusedError.

Not upstream.

